<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch 1997 grain area little changed from 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch 1997 grain area little changed from 1996.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch grain area in 1997 will be around 189,000 hectares, roughly unchanged from 1996, the government statistics office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The area is dominated by winter wheat, which will take up 124,400 hectares, down from 134,100 last year.</p>
<p>It made no forecast for the crop size.</p>
<p>The Netherlands produces around 1.5 million tonnes of grain a year, most of which is used domestically in animal feed production.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
